  id: S05_02
  era: "6th c. BCE \xB7 Section 5 \xB7 Mahajanapadas \xB7 c. 600 \u2013 321 BCE"
  title: 'Gana-sanghas: the republics'
  text: Some states, called gana-sanghas, were governed by assemblies of clan heads rather than a single king. The Vajji confederacy, with its capital at Vaishali, and the Mallas were prominent. Both the Buddha and Mahavira came from such clans.
